WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Okay, so now we're ready to open

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
the heart up and look at it. So I'm going

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.000
to go from the

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.000
front, and this has been dissected to

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.000
split it right down the middle, so you

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
can open it up like a book, and now we'll

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
look at some structures on the inside.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The first thing to notice is a large

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.000
piece of muscle, myocardium, that

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
separates the right ventricle from the

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.000
left ventricle. Notice that the right

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.000
ventricle has a thinner muscular wall

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.000
than the left ventricle, and that makes

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.000
sense because the left ventricle has to

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.000
pump blood out the aorta to the

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.000
entire body. The right ventricle only has

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.000
to pump it up to the lungs, which are

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.000
right next door.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:44.028
So you've got left atrium and left
